# Cloudflare Pages: static assets (JS bundles, robots.txt, sitemap.xml, og-image.png, ...) are
# matched before these rules run. The app's own pretty-URL routes have no static file of their
# own (web.output: "single", one index.html) so they need an explicit rewrite to the root at 200
# — NOT to /index.html: Cloudflare's own clean-URL layer auto-redirects any request that resolves
# to literally /index.html back to / (308), which turns a 200 rewrite into a redirect loop-breaker
# and (for a splat source) gets the whole rule silently disabled as an "infinite loop". Exact
# patterns are listed before splats per Cloudflare's own ordering guidance (static before dynamic).
# A path that matches none of these is real garbage, not a route this app knows: Cloudflare Pages
# serves public/404.html automatically for any unmatched path, at a real 404 — no redirect rule for
# that exists (404 isn't even a legal _redirects status; only 200/301/302/303/307/308 are).
/credits     /  200
/downloads   /  200
/import      /  200
/licenses    /  200
/privacy     /  200
/settings    /  200
/soundtrack  /  200
/book/*      /  200
/browse/*    /  200
